Rationale: output security needs ONE choke point every string passes before the engine draws it. In the React
host config, text instances (createTextInstance, commitTextUpdate), text-bearing props (content, title, value,
placeholder, StyledText chunks) and the setProperty default branch go through a host text filter; the Hub installs
prim/safe.ts: C0 controls other than TAB, CR and LF are drawn as their control pictures (ESC as ␛, so no escape
sequence is obeyed), DEL as ␡ and C1 controls as U+FFFD; bidi overrides and invisible format characters are
removed; links are limited to http/https. The host refuses to draw until a filter is set (fails closed with
TERM_UNSAFE_OUTPUT), so a build that forgets to install it shows nothing instead of passing raw bytes.

